/**
 * /home smoke (V3-P01; V3-SPEC §6.1, §10 P1) — HERMETIC: every same-origin /api/* and /gods-eye/* GET is
 * answered in the browser from the fixture world below (404 for what Home does not need), every non-GET is
 * REFUSED and counted (Home must never write), and the OSM tiles are aborted (the thumbs then show the
 * deck's own road network — the offline path is part of the check).
 *
 *   node tests/home-smoke.mjs [deckUrl]          (default http://127.0.0.1:5469; a dev deck of this tree)
 *
 * The fixture world (also imported by tests/home.unit.mjs): 4 decision units — an escort proposal that
 * expires in 48 s, a 108 corridor request, a decision-support proposal on a news-reported road accident,
 * a stolen vehicle with two pending sightings — 3 live operations, 3 planned events, 4 OSINT reports
 * (official · 2 news · unverified), 28 cameras, a GREEN city band, a simulated traffic feed. Road geometry,
 * cameras and junctions are copied from the int3cl sandbox; everything else is fictional. The raw mark
 * is exported so the smoke can prove it never reaches innerText without a named officer.
 *
 * Asserts:
 *   1. the page renders with zero page errors and sends ZERO non-GET requests;
 *   2. the featured decision is the soonest-deadline unit; the decision rail is in decisionUnits() order;
 *   3. counts equal the canonical selectors (window.__V3_HOME__.canonical = selectors.decisionUnits(),
 *      cardFigures): the decisions tile, the rail count, the rail's cards and the Decide badge agree; the
 *      reported / watchlisted tiles, the live and planned rails likewise;
 *   4. no raw registration mark in document.body.innerText without an officer (the masked one shows,
 *      with its lock); naming an officer through the V3 officer control (the v2 `duty-officer` input)
 *      shows the full mark; clearing the name masks it again;
 *   5. links: Review now and every decision card open the unit's V3 home (/decide/<kind>:<id>), never
 *      carrying a mark; the rail's Analyst opens `/analyst` (WORKSPACE); the OSM credit links the copyright page;
 *   6. accessibility: the first Tab stop is "Skip to main content"; ← / → move between cards in a rail;
 *      every map is role="img" with a label; the countdown is role="timer"; every <img> has alt;
 *   7. the offline map path: tiles refused → the thumbs draw the deck's road network;
 *   8. the alert list: a decision that starts waiting after load raises one unread alert (the bell);
 *   9. the language switch (in the top bar's one compact menu, never on the bar): हि turns <html lang> to hi and
 *      the hero button to Hindi.
 *
 * Exits 0 with `ok <name>` lines, 1 on any failure.
 */
